{"anchor": {"begin": [125, 0, 220.67], "end": [125, 0, 315.33], "env": "corollary", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 57, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "10.6", "source_sha256": "44e4fb5ea25b4517f36f58e841f74b5430c6f21117f940fad9b7368e3e03b52b", "statement": "Corollary 10.6. For every ν > 0, there is a smooth force on T3 × [0, ∞ ), compactly supported in time, for which the solution (U, P per ) of the periodic Navier–Stokes equations with viscosity ν and zero initial velocity is smooth on [0, 1) and satisfies lim sup t↑1 ∥U(t)∥ L ∞ ( T 3) = ∞ . Its velocity and pressure have support in a fixed compact subset of the interior of Q 0 at every time before one. There is no global smooth periodic solution for the same datum and force.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "high", "coverage": "full", "note": "periodic_corollary carries the whole corollary on unit-periodic lifts: a smooth periodic force vanishing for t ≤ 0 and after a finite time, fields smooth on [0, 1) with support in a compact subset of the open cube, unbounded speed near t = 1, and no global smooth periodic solution for the same datum and force (uniqueness of the maximal solution is not stated). The project's Comparator declaration navier_stokes_breakdown_periodic carries only the non-existence, in Fefferman's alternative (D) form, with a force that has polynomial time decay rather than compact time support.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.Comparator.ForceCondition": "9604ee2b70627406a043872f", "NavierStokes.Comparator.ForceCondition.mk": "fad7011c15e1911a0a95d83a", "NavierStokes.Comparator.ForceConditionPeriodic": "548c14ee7581d4da969c353e", "NavierStokes.Comparator.ForceConditionPeriodic.mk": "2b4c98d4e636446e068ab7ba", "NavierStokes.Comparator.InitialVelocityCondition": "83aa7d1989286d8318f23a37", "NavierStokes.Comparator.Ini